@ 43.3 - Proto-Uto-Aztecan to Luiseño
# citation: Radius Solis, from from Voegelin, Charles F., Florence M. Voegelin, & Kenneth L. Hale (1962), “Typological and Comparative Grammar of Uto-Aztecan: I (Phonology)”. International Journal of American Linguistics 28: Memoir 17 “[I]solated other instances of k → q occur with uncertain conditions”
	p > v / {V,ɨ}_ (the latter “sometimes”)
	p > v / “other conditions not known”
	t > l / medially
	t͡s > t͡ʃ
	k > q / #_V:[+low]
	k > q / a_
	k > x / a_
	ʔ > ∅ / #_
	s > ʃ
	l > n / medially
	o ɨ > e o
	V > ∅ / “in some final syllables (conditions are unknown and it varies by dialect)”